WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.660
How did your favorite Game of Thrones stars
really feel while they were filming some of

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.890
the most dramatic, intense moments in the
series?

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:10.420
Here are the scenes that the cast absolutely
dreaded filming -- and a few that certain

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.880
actors refused to take part in altogether.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.080
Warning: Season 8 spoilers ahead!

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.080
Cersei's "walk of shame" through King's Landing
in Season 5 was brutal enough to make audiences

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.140
sympathize with one of the most diabolical
characters in the entire show.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.760
To atone for the sin of adultery, Cersei was
forced to walk naked through King's Landing

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.500
while the citizens verbally and physically
assaulted her.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.400
Although many Game of Thrones stars are used
to wearing nothing but their birthday suits

00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:39.839
on camera, actress Lena Headey chose to work
with a body double for this scene rather than

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.480
baring it all.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.200
Headey said that the scene would have involved
three full days of shooting sans costume,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.580
and she didn't feel that she could accurately
portray Cersei's emotional state if she herself

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:51.159
was exposed the entire time.

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:55.530
Headey is also a mother, and she noted that
stripping down for certain scenes might bring

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.069
up some awkward conversations with her kids.

00:00:58.069 --> 00:01:02.479
Headey's usual stand-in, Rebecca Van Cleave,
agreed to appear nude in the scene, with Headey's

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:04.339
face superimposed on her body.

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:07.829
In response to claims that she was "less of
an actress" for preferring to keep herself

00:01:07.829 --> 00:01:10.000
covered, Headey had to stand up for herself.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.120
She told Entertainment Weekly,

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.119
The Game of Thrones Season 6 finale had every
fan on edge.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.800
The season went out with a bang — literally.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.420
Rather than attend her trial with the High
Sparrow, Cersei decided to pull off an unexpectedly

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.440
devious revenge plot.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.140
She set the entire Sept of Baelor ablaze with
wildfire, a highly flammable and rare substance

00:01:36.149 --> 00:01:39.210
that gives a whole new meaning to the phrase
"scorched earth."

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.280
Lancel Lannister tried to save the day in
vain — while in a tunnel under the Sept,

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.590
he notices three candles burning in a small
pool of wildfire, and he attempts to reach

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.399
the end of the tunnel as fast as he can to
blow them out.

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:54.130
Due to his injuries, he can only crawl, and
he does not make it in time.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.490
Actor Eugene Simon said this was his most
physically demanding scene.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:02.179
The directors had him spend the entire day
crawling, using only his upper body strength

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:02.700
throughout.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:03.300
He told Elle,

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.200
Euron Greyjoy is one of the most frightening
characters of Game of Thrones.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.210
He has no moral compass, and there seems to
be nothing he won't do in pursuit of the power

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.390
that he craves.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.370
Even among the other ruthless Game of Thrones
characters, Euron possesses a unique form

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:23.900
of evil.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.660
Actor Pilou Asbæk plays the role perfectly,
yet in real life, Asbæk is nowhere near as

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.000
frightening; in fact, he was actually intimidated
by one scene in particular.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.640
In the Game of Thrones universe, every kingdom
has their own unique rituals and ceremonies.

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:42.260
When a new king is crowned in the Iron Islands,
a drowning ceremony is part of their initiation.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.970
Of course, filming something like this is
complicated, and there's no way that the cast

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.930
and crew are going to get it right in one
take.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.189
Asbæk said that filming the drowning scene
was quite a struggle.

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:54.730
After all, it's not easy to act while you're
freezing cold and unable to breathe.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.960
Asbæk told Elle,

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.920
"What is dead may never die."

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.620
Wearing unique costumes and makeup on set
is just part of the deal on Game of Thrones.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:17.550
To create some of the special aesthetic effects,
actors have had to wear colored contacts and

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.500
prosthetic lenses.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.599
For example, after Arya Stark goes temporarily
blind in Season 5, Maisie Williams had to

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:27.530
wear colored contact lenses for a few episodes
until her sight was restored.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:30.830
But she's not the only actor on set who had
to spend a little time in the dark.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.150
For Meryn Trant's death scene in Season 5,
the cast and crew began shooting early in

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.960
the morning, and actor Ian Beattie recalls
getting prosthetics in his eyes around 9AM

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.460
that day.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.640
Unfortunately, the prosthetics basically left
him blind for a full day of shooting, and

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.129
he had to leave them in for a full 12 hours.

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:51.129
He says that all he remembers from that particular
day of shooting was total darkness from morning

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:52.129
until night.

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:54.700
He remembers his death scene as his biggest
challenge on set.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:55.879
Beattie told Elle,

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:58.230
"It was in many ways quite a surreal day.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.840
It was very technical, but Maisie and I had
worked it out in the rehearsals, and we were

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.380
ready."

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:08.280
Tormund Giantsbane is a fan favorite on Game
of Thrones – although he is arguably a relatively

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.739
minor character, he's gotten more and more
screen time throughout his tenure on the series,

00:04:11.739 --> 00:04:15.440
to the point that it raised something of a
fan uproar when his fate was left ambiguous

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.080
in the Season 7 finale.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.680
He's a tough character who may be gruff at
times, but beneath his rough exterior, there's

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.360
something endearing about him.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.840
Actor Kristofer Hivju has appeared in plenty
of crazy battle scenes where it seems like

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.460
it's hard to keep track of anything happening
onscreen.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.970
Hivju admits that by the time he was scheduled
to shoot the Season 7 finale, he'd had enough

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.400
of working with the wights.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.180
The wights that audiences see are actually
a small crowd of extras, with the majority

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.140
added digitally in post-production.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:45.580
Regardless, the actors had to keep up with
quick choreography, and according to Hivju,

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.660
the scene pushed him to his physical limits.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.180
He told Elle,

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.080
"In the beginning, it was tough, but in the
end it became a kind of horrible dance.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.560
It was extremely exhausting: They just kept
coming, kept coming, kept coming."

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.620
Ellaria Sand and her daughter Tyene had one
of the most frightening death scenes in the

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.320
entire series — and not a drop of blood
was spilled.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.360
Cersei handcuffs both Ellaria and Tyene to
opposite walls of a dungeon, and then poisons

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.320
Tyene as revenge for the murder of her daughter
Myrcellla, forcing Ellaria to

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:12.170
watch her own daughter die while she is helplessly
stuck.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:16.790
To make matters worse, Cersei promises to
keep Ellaria alive for some time, solely for

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.920
the purpose of torturing her and prolonging
her suffering.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.630
Ellaria actress Indira Varma
said that she and Rosabell Sellers, who played

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.290
Tyene, struggled with their handcuffs throughout
the entire day of filming — since they were

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:31.330
supposed to fight against them, the cuffs
would occasionally come undone, but at other

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.870
times, they got stuck in them.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.990
Varma was one of the last people on set that
day, and she found herself unable to get out

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:37.990
of the cuffs.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.070
Finally, a crew member from the props department
discovered a solution.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.070
Varma said in an episode of Games Revealed,

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.980
"Literally, at the end of the day, I was like,
'Mate, I can't get it off, can someone help

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.100
me?' and everyone's gone.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:52.140
"Pete from props is like, 'I think we need
a saw,' and I had to be sawn out."

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.620
Emilia Clarke said that filming Daenerys'
final scenes was heavy, but one scene much

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.060
earlier in the series really pushed her to
her limits as an actor.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.140
In Season 1, Daenerys eats a horse heart during
a Dothraki [Doth-RACK-ee] ceremony.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.610
The scene looked painfully realistic, and
many viewers probably wondered what Clarke

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:11.230
was actually eating — whatever it was, it
couldn't have tasted that great.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:14.840
Clarke wasn't chowing down on real, bloody
meat, but the "feast" wasn't much more appetizing.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.640
"She has to eat the whole heart?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.160
Hope that wasn't my horse."

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.600
"She's doing well."

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.590
The horse heart was actually made out of solidified
jam, and Clarke said the flavor reminded her

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.980
of a nasty combination of bleach and raw pasta.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.680
In fact, she said she was so grossed out by
the taste that she barely felt like she had

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.160
to act in the scene.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:37.870
And unfortunately, this was not the kind of
scene that she could just get over with in

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.270
one take — shooting lasted for several days,
and Clarke said that she was physically ill.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.270
She told The Mirror,

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:46.920
"I ate roughly 28 hearts throughout the days
we filmed that scene.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.220
Fortunately, they gave me a spit bucket because
I was vomiting in it quite often."

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:54.990
When Jon Snow and Daenerys finally met in
Season 7, it was obvious that there was a

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:58.750
spark of instant chemistry between the two
characters, and anyone could have predicted

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.500
that they would fall for each other.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.930
Romance was definitely on the horizon.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:05.940
At first, it seemed like destiny — fire
and ice were coming together at last.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.370
But in true Game of Thrones fashion, they
couldn't simply hook up and then live happily

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:10.220
ever after.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.800
Unbeknownst to either of them, Jon is actually
a Targaryen by birth, and Daenerys is his

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.300
aunt.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.680
Needless to say, actor Kit Harington had some
mixed feelings about the scene.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.750
After years of working on the show, Harington
and Clarke are good friends, and filming a

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:26.300
romantic scene together was undoubtedly going
to be a little bit awkward.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.610
Plus, knowing their characters' family lineage,
Harington thought that Jon and Daenerys were

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:31.650
making a mistake.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.950
Both actors relied on humor to keep the situation
a little more lighthearted.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:38.940
"I like looking at her and going, 'Oh, God,
I'm sorry!"

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:42.091
Throughout Game of Thrones, so many different
characters have come and gone, and there are

00:07:42.091 --> 00:07:46.200
always several major storylines going on throughout
the known world, so it's only expected that

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.840
some major characters rarely appear in scenes
together.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:52.510
For the most recent seasons, this has been
the case for Bronn and Cersei.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:56.270
But it's not because their characters don't
have any connection — after all, Bronn spends

00:07:56.270 --> 00:08:01.010
plenty of time with Jamie Lannister, Cersei's
twin brother and not-so-secret lover.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:05.820
It's actually because Bronn actor Jerome Flynn
and Lena Headey used to date, and the breakup

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.950
must have been fairly tumultuous, because
both actors refuse to film scenes together.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:14.340
Flynn and Headey nearly had to share a scene
in Season 7, when almost all of the main characters

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.300
convened at the Dragon Pit summit.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:20.050
However, attentive viewers may have noticed
that Bronn and Cersei didn't even share a

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:24.450
second of screen time — Bronn made a quick
exit and excused himself for a drink before

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.640
Cersei arrived.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:29.961
Although the two split before late 2014, when
Headey began dating her current partner, the

00:08:29.961 --> 00:08:31.480
wounds must still feel fresh.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:35.200
But perhaps they will have to set their differences
aside for the final season.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.840
After all, Bronn is now supposed to be leading
the Lannister army and working for Cersei,

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:43.080
so it will be interesting to see how the directors
work around this dilemma.

